too late as Risztov held on for the gold medal in 1-57:38.2, only 4/10ths of a second ahead of the American. Grimaldi came in three seconds later, holding off Payne for the bronze medal. Anderson’s silver medal came one week after her sister, " [:a {:href "/athletes/126697"} "Alyssa Anderson"] ", had won a gold medal in the 4×200 relay as a prelim swimmer for the United States."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Lap 1"] [:th {} "Lap 2"] [:th {} "Lap 3"] [:th {} "Lap 4"] [:th {} "Lap 5"] [:th {} "Lap 2 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 3 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 4 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 5 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 6 Split"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93520"} "Éva Risztov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1-57:38.2"] [:td {} "19:22.2 (1)"] [:td {} "39:09.3 (3)"] [:td {} "59:09.4 (1)"] [:td {} "1-18:58.8 (1)"] [:td {} "1-38:32.3 (1)"] [:td {} "19:47.1 (9)"] [:td {} "20:00.1 (3)"] [:td {} "19:49.4 (8)"] [:td {} "19:33.5 (3)"] [:td {} "19:05.9 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126698"} "Haley Anderson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1-57:38.6"] [:td {} "19:22.9 (4)"] [:td {} "39:07.4 (1)"] [:td {} "59:12.2 (3)"] [:td {} "1-19:01.2 (3)"] [:td {} "1-38:35.6 (3)"] [:td {} "19:44.5 (1)"] [:td {} "20:04.8 (=16)"] [:td {} "19:49.0 (7)"] [:td {} "19:34.4 (=4)"] [:td {} "19:03.0 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/at